SCOPE OF SERVICES
The proposed scope of services is in response discussions with the client.
Based on Terra con's understanding of thesite, the project crosses an area identified by
the Wyoming Department of Environmental Quality(WDEQ)as the Former Cheyenne
Steam Laundry.Based ona Site Characterization Report dated October 9,2014
prepared by Terracon, concentrations of tetra chlo roe the ne(PCE)were reported in soil
and groundwater in the vicinity of thesite.
Materials Management Plan (MMP)
Terra con will prepare an MMPtoassist with the management of subsurface media
potentially impacted with the identified chemicals of concern, including PCE.TheMMP
will provide best management practices for site safety, site control/security，and
contaminated soil/groundwater contingency procedures including soil segregation,
stockpile management, and soil stockpile characterization.Inaddition, theplan will
provide direction on theproper disposition(ifwarranted)of soil and/or groundwater to
bedisturbed，in theformof laboratory analysis required forwaste characterization
and/orprofiling the waste materials for disposal attheproper and authorized facility.
3.0SCHEDULE
Services will be initiated uponreceipt of the written notice to proceed.The MMP will be
submitted to the client within30business days of authorization toproceed.
